# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values you need. Everything except
# API_KEY is optional; unset providers just get skipped by the auto-detect
# precedence (Anthropic → OpenRouter → Groq → Gemini → Ollama).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Required — authenticates API requests via the X-Api-Key header.
API_KEY=change-me-to-a-strong-key

# Alternative to API_KEY — path to a file containing the key (Docker secrets, mounted volumes).
# ApiKeyFile=/run/secrets/travel-planner-api-key

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LLM provider credentials — set at least one. See README for provider notes.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPEN_ROUTER_AI_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Ollama endpoint (local); default is http://localhost:11434 when unset.
OLLAMA_HOST=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-provider model overrides. Uncomment to pin a specific model without a
# code change. Defaults live in Services/ChatClientFactory.cs.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-20250514
# OPEN_ROUTER_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-chat
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.1-8b-instant
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen3-coder:30b

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Router split — routes to a cheaper client per turn for route classification.
# Both are optional; if only ROUTER_MODEL is set, provider defaults to the
# auto-detected main provider.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ROUTER_PROVIDER=anthropic
# ROUTER_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Conversation persistence.
# Backend: Sqlite (default) or InMemory (ephemeral, for tests/demos).
# ConnectionString points to the SQLite file; defaults to conversations.db in
# the working directory. In Docker Compose this is /app/data/conversations.db.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Conversations__Backend=Sqlite
# ConnectionStrings__Conversations=Data Source=/app/data/conversations.db

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OpenTelemetry (opt-in). Set the OTLP endpoint of a self-hosted collector
# (Grafana Tempo, Jaeger, OpenTelemetry Collector, etc.). When unset, spans
# stay in-process and cost nothing.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://tempo.internal:4317
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=LocalAgentTravelPlanner

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Continuous SQLite replication via the Litestream sidecar. Only required when
# running `docker compose --profile backup up`. Supports any Litestream backend
# (s3://, gs://, abs://, sftp://, file://) — on-prem deployments typically use
# sftp://backup-nas.internal/... or file:///mnt/backups/....
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LITESTREAM_REPLICA_URL=sftp://backup-nas.internal/replicas/travel-planner
# LITESTREAM_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# LITESTREAM_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
